WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 039. A TRACE IS EVIDENCE—NOT THE TRUTH. An event log can show sequence and state without proving intent, correctness, completeness, causation, or a safe outcome.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
BOUND THE SESSION. PURPOSE · AUTHORITY · SCOPE · STOP. Lock agent and model version, environment, permitted tools and data, accountable owner, approval gates, prohibited actions, and termination conditions.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
CAPTURE SAFELY. EVENT · TIME · STATE · RESULT. Use synthetic redacted traces. Record requests, tool outcomes, approvals, errors, retries, and side effects—never credentials, secrets, or private content.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
KEEP LAYERS APART. OBSERVED ≠ INFERRED ≠ VERIFIED. Preserve provenance, missing events, uncertainty, contradictions, transformations, and reviewer notes instead of inventing a continuous story.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
INSPECT THE CONTROL. REPLAY · CONTAIN · CORRECT · VALIDATE. Check permissions, sequence, human intervention, external change, stop behavior, and consequence before deciding whether work can stand.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. INSPECTABLE WITHOUT EXPOSURE. ACCOUNTABLE AGENT WORK LEAVES AN INSPECTABLE TRAIL WITHOUT EXPOSING PRIVATE CONTENT.

